/*	Welcome to Terrains.json, world's best hash/keys since 0xD!

	Being a TC basemod, mod explorers might want a bit more description on the internals. 
	Base terrains are mostly the same as G&K:
		Flatland =~ Plains, w/ features/Grass overlay, by default used w/ paths on Grassland
		+ Surf = Usually found between Coast and Ocean as a water mid-body
		+ Coast|Surf shore: non- /edges clones of themselves for shoreline decors
		+ Rough Ocean: Vis blocking ocean tiles, w/ specific buff/de-buffs
		- Lakes: May add specific Lake terrain for Lost Lake etc
		- Tundra: No related use
		Snow =~ Snow, only one default instance atm, glass sword, also may apply to Stonegate and other deep mountain areas like Avatar island
	Then TerrainFeatures:
		Swamp =~ Marsh, basically the same thing
		Hills = Hill, but might restore this name due to easing map conversion
		+ Scrub: light vegetation
		+ Woods =~ Forest
		Forest: Heavier density
		Thicket =~ Jungle, more apt naming for a European fantasy setting
		- Ice,Atoll
		- Flood plains, possibly for bridges/ as underbody TF
	Finally TerrainDecor:
		+ bridges/
		+ paths/
		+ rivers/ - a mapdev trickplay, requiring placing actual river as guides then rivers/ decor to follow river flows
	Special assets:
		features/ - for ruleVariant terrain render layering, or other indirect tile render assets

*/ //////// Base terrains ////////

